14 TL
(GUI Explanation for Professor - Bearing Fault Diagnosis Project) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Purpose of the GUI) Tj
T*
(This GUI demonstrates bearing fault diagnosis in a practical way. It takes vibration signal data as input,) Tj
T*
(extracts important features, and uses the trained machine learning model to predict the bearing condition.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Input Settings) Tj
T*
(Sampling Rate \(Hz\): Number of amplitude samples recorded per second. It is needed for time scaling and FFT.) Tj
T*
(Upload Vibration CSV: Uploads a CSV file containing vibration amplitude values.) Tj
T*
(Use Built-In Demo Signal: Tests the system using a prepared example signal.) Tj
T*
(Expected Classes: Normal, Inner Race Fault, Outer Race Fault, Ball Fault.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Workflow Section) Tj
T*
(A vibration signal is uploaded. Then the system computes time-domain and FFT-based features and sends) Tj
T*
(them to the trained machine learning model for classification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Predicted Fault) Tj
T*
(This shows the final bearing condition predicted by the trained model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Confidence) Tj
T*
(This is the probability score of the predicted class. Higher value means the model is more confident.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Signal Length) Tj
T*
(This shows how many amplitude samples are present in the uploaded signal window.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Time-Domain Waveform) Tj
T*
(This graph shows amplitude versus time and represents the raw vibration behavior of the bearing signal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8. Frequency Spectrum \(FFT\)) Tj
T*
(This graph shows magnitude versus frequency after FFT and helps identify dominant frequency components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Confidence by Fault Type) Tj
T*
(This table shows the probability of the signal belonging to each fault category.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Extracted Features) Tj
T*
(This section shows numerical features extracted from the vibration signal, such as mean, standard deviation,) Tj
T*
(RMS, kurtosis, spectral mean, and frequency variation factor. These features are used as input to the classifier.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Confusion Matrix) Tj
T*
(This shows model performance on test data. Diagonal values are correct predictions and off-diagonal values) Tj
T*
(are misclassifications.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. Feature Importance) Tj
T*
(This shows which extracted features are most important for the Random Forest model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13. Backend Flow) Tj
T*
(After uploading the CSV, the system reads the amplitude values, extracts features, passes them to the) Tj
T*
(trained model, predicts the most likely fault type, and displays the result in the GUI.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(14. Short Overall Explanation) Tj
T*
(This GUI is the practical front-end of the bearing fault diagnosis system. It takes vibration data as input,) Tj
T*
(extracts meaningful features, classifies the bearing condition using a trained ML model, and displays the) Tj
T*
(result along with signal plots and model interpretation outputs.) Tj
ET
